WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.822
API security protects the interfaces that
expose application data,

2
00:00:07.902 --> 00:00:12.321
business logic, and service operations.

3
00:00:12.401 --> 00:00:20.228
APIs connect users, devices, services,
partners, and internal systems.

4
00:00:20.308 --> 00:00:28.767
That makes them essential to modern
software and also makes them a direct path to

5
00:00:28.847 --> 00:00:30.993
sensitive actions.

6
00:00:31.073 --> 00:00:39.657
A secure API is not simply reachable over
HTTPS or hidden behind a user interface.

7
00:00:39.737 --> 00:00:47.060
It is explicit about identity, access,
input, output, abuse limits,

8
00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:50.296
and operational visibility.

9
00:00:50.376 --> 00:00:56.436
Strong API security starts with clear
trust boundaries.

10
00:00:56.516 --> 00:01:05.479
Know which endpoints are public,
partner-facing, internal, service-to-service,

11
00:01:05.559 --> 00:01:07.705
or webhook-driven.

12
00:01:07.785 --> 00:01:14.981
Know where tokens are validated, where
authorization is enforced,

13
00:01:15.061 --> 00:01:22.510
where request contracts are checked, and
where responses are shaped.

14
00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:26.882
Authentication identifies the caller,

15
00:01:26.962 --> 00:01:36.052
but authorization decides whether the
caller can perform the requested operation on

16
00:01:36.132 --> 00:01:42.192
the specific resource in the specific
tenant or context.

17
00:01:42.272 --> 00:01:51.614
Validation, response design, and abuse
controls reduce both security and reliability

18
00:01:51.694 --> 00:01:52.325
risk.

19
00:01:52.405 --> 00:02:00.611
APIs should validate fields, formats,
ranges, arrays, unknown properties,

20
00:02:00.691 --> 00:02:06.498
and request sizes before data reaches
sensitive code.

21
00:02:06.578 --> 00:02:12.133
Responses should return only what the
caller needs.

22
00:02:12.213 --> 00:02:18.778
Rate limits, quotas, pagination limits,
resource controls,

23
00:02:18.858 --> 00:02:27.947
and replay-aware workflows help APIs
remain dependable under automation pressure.

24
00:02:28.027 --> 00:02:36.612
The final takeaway is that API security is
an operational discipline as much as an

25
00:02:36.692 --> 00:02:39.091
implementation task.

26
00:02:39.171 --> 00:02:43.842
Logs, tests, specifications, monitoring,

27
00:02:43.922 --> 00:02:51.370
and regular review keep endpoints
understandable as systems change.

28
00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:58.646
The goal is to make every API endpoint
explicit, least-privileged,

29
00:02:58.726 --> 00:03:04.660
validated, observable, and resilient
against misuse.
